the two partitions share NO jump point in this range, so neither refines the
other. one width ladder cannot key both. a design needs two ladders, or one
over the common refinement, which is strictly larger than either.

16's verdict that the access width is not a third OUTPUT stands: it is a function
of W. what it costs is a second rung partition, which 16 did not name and which is
not free, because the ladder is the part of the derivation the design has already
refused to enumerate.
